{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789833922,"nonce":"wGt/nN/7ZY58beZR/NKqKqlZQ4Q=","title":"SSA construction walks the function once per collapsed phi","message":"Three superlinear steps in `SsaBuilder::build_from_typed_cfg`, all\nproportional to the number of phis times the size of the function:\n\n- `substitute_value` walked every instruction, terminator and phi for\n  each placeholder phi that resolved to a single value, and each trivial\n  phi `collapse_trivial_phis` removed (which also walked every block's\n  phi list per phi). nqueens' module body, comprehension-heavy with 14\n  loop headers, took 64 ms to lower; 54% of its SSA time was in\n  `substitute_value`.\n- `current_preds_of` scanned every block's terminator per recursive\n  variable read, although the predecessor lists had just been recomputed\n  from the terminators.\n- `edge_is_back` computed the function's dominator tree per\n  self-referencing phi incoming.\n- `read_variable` read `ZYNTAX_SSA_TRACE` from the environment twice\n  per call.\n\nFix: substitutions are recorded and applied to the function in one pass\n(at the end of phi filling and once per collapse round), reads resolve\nthrough the pending map meanwhile; the recomputed edges are trusted\nuntil a block is wired; the dominator tree is cached while the CFG\nstands still; the trace switch is read once.\n\nnqueens compile phase 97 -\u003e 37 ms; parse_args (204 blocks) 3.3 ms -\u003e\nabout 2.","files":null}]}